name: sim.unpackUInt32Table
description: Unpacks a string (or part of it) into an array of uint32 numbers
luaSynopsis: list uint32Numbers = sim.unpackUInt32Table(bytes data, int startUint32Index = 0, int uint32Count = 0, int additionalByteOffset = 0)
pythonSynopsis: int[] uint32Numbers = sim.unpackUInt32Table(buffer data, int startUint32Index = 0, int uint32Count = 0, int additionalByteOffset = 0)
inputs:
1. data: string (values between 0 and 255) that contains packed uint32 numbers
2. startUint32Index: zero-based index from which on data should be unpacked (from data[4*startUint32Index+1+additionalByteOffset]). Can be omitted in which case 0 is used
3. uint32Count: amount of uint32s that should be unpacked. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum of uint32s should be unpacked from the indicated startUint32Index)
4. additionalByteOffset: byte offset that will be added before reading the uint32s. Can be omitted, in which case 0 is used.
outputs:
1. integerNumbers: array containing unpacked uint32 numbers
replacedBy:
- name: unpackArray, class: app, file: app_unpackArray.method
